    "body": "Nits:\n\n- I would expect \"`rgba-unorm8`\" and \"`rgba-float16`\". This would better match the existing names and would match https://w3ctag.github.io/design-principles/#casing-rules.\n- Why not use `ImageDataArray` in the existing constructor?\n- You call it both \"`rgba16unorm`\" and \"`rgba16float`\".\n\nI think you also need to adjust how existing algorithms will deal with this newish `ImageData` type. E.g., `putImageData()` assumes a color value per byte.",
