    "updated_at": "2025-02-14T11:24:29Z",
    "body": "Thanks! Just pushed https://github.com/ccameron-chromium/ColorWeb-CG/commit/a3c6a70557f098252583f829aee85c0bd382ba90\n\n> * I would expect \"`rgba-unorm8`\" and \"`rgba-float16`\". This would better match the existing names and would match https://w3ctag.github.io/design-principles/#casing-rules.\n\nGood point.\n\nThis will not match the [WebGPU enums](https://www.w3.org/TR/webgpu/#enumdef-gputextureformat). I consider this a feature, cause I don't want people to sloppily copy enums across, and it doesn't match WebGL or 2D either.\n\n> * Why not use `ImageDataArray` in the existing constructor?\n\nCause I hadn't thought of that :). Updated the explainer.\n\n> * You call it both \"`rgba16unorm`\" and \"`rgba16float`\".\n\nOops, fixed.\n\n> I think you also need to adjust how existing algorithms will deal with this newish `ImageData` type. E.g., `putImageData()` assumes a color value per byte.\n\nYikes!\n\nThe spec says \"writes data from ImageData structures back to the rendering context's output bitmap\". That was never accurate. `ImageData` has always been unpremultiplied and 2D canvas has always been premultiplied, so there has always been that conversion performed. There is also color conversion performed (although that is more recent). Type conversion will be another breaking of this.\n\nIn practice, `putImageData` should never have existed, and `ImageData` should have been \n a [`CanvasImageSource`](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#canvasimagesource). Maybe I should open an issue on making that change (we aren't removing `putImageData`, but we can change the spec to say it's equivalent to a saveState-resetState-drawImage-restoreState call sequence).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
